# S2 (plan 16) — THE CLIENT'S VOXEL CACHE IS THE SERVER'S, BY THE FORMAT'S OWN CRC.
#
# The client caches every terrain layer it is streamed and still draws the SERVER's
# meshes. That is the point of the step rather than a half-measure: with the cache
# beside a picture it does not affect, a disagreement is a NUMBER long before
# anything depends on the cache being right — and a step that switched the drawing
# over at the same time could not tell a bad cache from a bad mesher.
#
# ⚠ THE CHECKSUM IS `world_save`'s, NOT ONE INVENTED FOR THE WIRE. Two sides that
# agree on a hash they made up agree about the wrong thing; this way "the client
# matches the server" and "the client would survive a round trip" are one claim.
#
# ⚠ CONTROL, SEEN RED: perturbing ONE cell of ONE layer in `layer_wire` gives
# `agree 23 bad 1` — one layer disagreeing, and exactly one. `hex_world`'s own
# `layer_wire.loft` pins the half that makes that possible: one changed cell moves
# the checksum. Without it this row would pass on a constant.
rate 0
at 0 0 0
key ArrowUp
wait rebuilt
step 20
snap s2-cache
step 20
wait cache
